.TH DLUP 1 "2026" "dlup @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dlup \- download media with yt\-dlp and push it straight to an rclone remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dlup
\fB\-r\fR \fIREMOTE\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIURL\fR...
.br
.B dlup
\fB\-r\fR \fIREMOTE\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]... \fB\-f\fR \fILIST\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each URL,
.B dlup
downloads it with
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
into a staging directory, uploads what landed there to an
.BR rclone (1)
remote, and removes the local copy before moving to the next one. One video at
a time, so a long list never fills the disk.
.PP
Each URL gets its own staging directory. That matters: picking "the newest file
in the download folder" guesses wrong the moment a download produces more than
one file, or the folder has anything left over in it.
.PP
A URL that fails to download, or that downloads nothing, is counted and
skipped; the rest of the list still runs. A URL whose upload fails keeps its
local copy so the transfer can be retried by hand, and the path is printed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remote " " \fIREMOTE\fR
rclone destination, for example \fBgdrive:Recordings\fR. Required, unless it
comes from the config file or
.BR $DLUP_REMOTE .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cookies " " \fIFILE\fR
Cookie file to hand to yt\-dlp, for sites that only serve the media to a
signed\-in session.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Staging directory. Default \fB~/.cache/dlup\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-from\-file " " \fILIST\fR
Read URLs from a file, one per line. Blank lines and everything from a \fB#\fR
onwards are ignored, so the list can be commented.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Concurrent fragments per download. Default \fB5\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-retries " " \fIN\fR
Retries per download. Default \fB10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep the local copy after a successful upload.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would happen and transfer nothing.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/dlup/config
Shell\-style \fBkey=value\fR lines. Recognised keys: \fBremote\fR,
\fBcookies\fR, \fBdir\fR, \fBjobs\fR, \fBretries\fR.
.PP
Precedence, strongest first: command\-line options, the config file, then the
environment.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DLUP_REMOTE
Default rclone remote.
.TP
.B DLUP_COOKIES
Default cookie file.
.TP
.B DLUP_DIR
Default staging directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every URL downloaded and uploaded.
.TP
.B 1
At least one URL failed.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage, or yt\-dlp or rclone is missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
One video:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dlup \-r gdrive:Recordings https://example.com/video
.EE
.RE
.PP
A commented list, behind a login:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dlup \-r gdrive:Recordings \-c ~/cookies.txt \-f links.txt
.EE
.RE
.PP
With the remote in the config file, so it never has to be typed:
.PP
.RS
.EX
printf 'remote=gdrive:Recordings\\n' > ~/.config/dlup/config
dlup https://example.com/video
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR rclone (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @MAINTAINER@.
